        "title": "fix(parallel): use truncateUtf16Safe for MCP error JSON truncation",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- **Problem**: `extractMcpToolPayload()` in `extensions/parallel/src/parallel-mcp-search.runtime.ts` uses naive `.slice(0, 500)` on JSON-serialized error and result objects, which can split UTF-16 surrogate pairs when the content contains emoji or other multi-codepoint characters.\n- **Solution**: Replace `.slice(0, 500)` with `truncateUtf16Safe(JSON.stringify(...), 500)` at three call sites to preserve surrogate pair integrity.\n- **What changed**: Three call sites in `extractMcpToolPayload` + added import.\n- **What did NOT change**: No API, config, or behavior change. The truncation length (500 characters) is preserved. Error messages are thrown with the same content (minus surrogate pair corruption).\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior addressed**: String truncation that may split UTF-16 surrogate pairs in JSON-serialized error and result text included in Parallel MCP error messages shown to users.\n- **Real environment tested**: TypeScript compilation check — the change is mechanical and `truncateUtf16Safe` correctness is independently verified in `packages/normalization-core/src/utf16-slice.test.ts`.\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch**: Three `.slice(0, 500)` call sites are replaced with `truncateUtf16Safe(..., 500)`. `truncateUtf16Safe` from `openclaw/plugin-sdk/text-utility-runtime` is already imported in sibling file `parallel-search-normalize.ts` in the same package.\n- **After-fix evidence**: `truncateUtf16Safe` is already used in the same extension package (`extensions/parallel/src/parallel-search-normalize.ts`) and across 13+ merged PRs.\n- **Observed result after the fix**: For BMP text the output is identical; for text with surrogate pairs at the boundary, the surrogate pair is preserved instead of corrupted.\n- **What was not tested**: No real Parallel Search MCP invocation with surrogate-pair content. The change is mechanically identical to the 13+ already-merged PRs.\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- **merge-risk**: Low. Three call-sites, same pattern merged 13+ times. No new dependencies, no config changes, no API changes.\n- **Mitigations**: `truncateUtf16Safe` has standalone unit tests in `normalization-core`. Zero behavioral change for ASCII/BMP text paths.\n- Size: XS\n\n## AI-assisted\n\nThis PR was generated with Claude Code.",
